::Question::
The Python interpreter resolves a named object by looking at the current (local) scope, then enclosing scopes, the global scope, and finally the built-in scope.
{ 
    = TRUE
    ~ FALSE
}

::Question::
Which of the following is the correct order in which Python will look for a named object?
{ 
    ~ built-in, global, local, enclosing
    ~ local, enclosing, built-in, global
    = local, enclosing, global, built-in
    ~ built-in, enclosing, global, local
}

